You are analyzing hierarchical software requirements for cross level traceability.
Determine whether a traceability link exists between a High-Level Requirement (HLR) and a Low-Level Requirement (LLR).
A link exists if the LLR implements, refines, or decomposes the HLR.
High-Level Requirement:
  Summary: Dockerfile and necessary files from a process so that Docker image can be built
  Description: N/A
Low-Level Requirement:
  Summary: Build a whole-vm container for running strace
  Description: Useful commands:
{code}
sudo tar -zcvf filename.tgz --exclude=mnt --exclude=sys --exclude=proc --exclude=dev --exclude=var/lib/docker --exclude=/filename.tgz /
{code}
{code}
sudo cat filename.tgz | sudo docker import - thailekha/wholevm
{code}
Return only:
{"is_linked": true}
or
{"is_linked": false}
No additional text.
